  "behavior": [
    "successEnabled is an independent default-off preference; old enabled remains attention reminders, with shared sound and system permission facts.",
    "Only actual send admission creates a success candidate. Official done/end_turn is reconciled with the real projected ending, no failed or pending tools/compactions, pending permissions, uncertain connection or unfinished official asynchronous task. History replay and prose do not establish success.",
    "In-memory dedup and exact current thread/connection/session/end ownership prevent duplicate or stale work notifications. Work view visibility alone does not retire the owner.",
    "Pending submission attempts share bounded exact rendererNonce/sequence withdrawal. The real thread store publishes retirement synchronously, including removal of the original object. Approval/question expiry after submit begins also withdraws. Interrupted notices are not assumed resolved from UI recovery.",
    "A submit timeout remains uncertain and retains retirement until owner invalidation. No automatic resubmission. withdrawn means the backend ticket had not crossed its dispatch boundary; alreadySubmitted means the submission call began, not that the OS accepted or displayed it; unknown never proves suppression.",
    "Existing click target navigation and foreground/system gates are reused. New backend platform gates and real system presentation are peer/root responsibilities."
  ],
